    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "[Please download the \"README.txt\" file for instructions] \n        \n        We present the Stanford I2V dataset, a large-scale dataset which is useful for research on the problem of querying a video database using images. We have collected more than 3,800 hours of newscast videos and annotated more than 200 ground-truth queries. The dataset can be visually explored at http://blackhole1.stanford.edu/vidsearch/dataset/stanfordi2v.html . \n        \n        We also introduce the Video Bookmarking dataset, which makes use of the same database videos as the Stanford I2V dataset, but introducing a different query set. The application modeled by this dataset corresponds to the case where a user is interested in retrieving the video being played using a picture of a display, e.g., to resume playback in a different device.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "A. Araujo, J. Chaves, D. Chen, R. Angst, and B. Girod, “Stanford I2V: A News Video Dataset for Query-by-Image Experiments,” in Proc. ACM Multimedia Systems Conference, 2015.",
